                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 3]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Counselor of Embassy in Belgium</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sussdorff</hi>)</head>
                <p>In a further note, dated November 19, 1936, the British Government addressed
                    certain supplementary views to the Governments of Belgium, France, Germany and
                    Italy on the basis of the communication of views contained in the notes of the
                    four Governments. In its note of November 19, 1936, the British Government
                    raised the following points: <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>In the proposed Western Pact it asked for a guarantee for Great
                            Britain from both France and Germany.</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>Question of the aggressor. The British Government again expressed the
                            opinion that only one body is adapted to deciding this question—namely,
                            the Council of the League of Nations.</item>
                        <label>(3)</label>
                        <item>Insistence was again laid on the importance of a subsequent meeting of
                            other interested Powers in the event of the settlement of the question
                            of a new Western Pact.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
            </div>
